imx95-navqb: add Neutron NPU DMA pool (reserved-memory)

The base imx95.dtsi neutron node ships with no memory-region and the NavQ board
dts does not assign one, so the Neutron NPU has no dedicated DMA pool. Add a
reserved shared-dma-pool and bind it to the neutron node.

NavQ95 has >=8 GiB and u-boot fixes up the memory node at runtime, so a 4 GiB
pool at 0x1_0000_0000 fits above the existing reservations with no collision.
"reusable" makes it a shared-dma CMA pool, available to the system until the NPU
claims it.

Regenerated for the wrynose imx95-navq-lf-6.18.y kernel: the driver already
carries the stock IRQ-completion path (so the walnascar 0002 backport is dropped),
but the neutron node still lacks a memory-region. Appended at the end of the board
dts. HARDWARE-UNVERIFIED on wrynose.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [NavQ95 board integration; should be fixed in NXP-Robotics/linux-imx]
Signed-off-by: Leonardo Bornia <leonardo.bornia@toradex.com>

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx95-navqb.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx95-navqb.dts
@@ -1646,3 +1646,15 @@
 	boot = <&vpu_boot>;
 	sram = <&sram1>;
 };
+
+&{/reserved-memory} {
+	neutron_mem: neutron_memory@100000000 {
+		compatible = "shared-dma-pool";
+		reusable;
+		reg = <0x1 0x00000000 0x1 0x00000000>;
+	};
+};
+
+&neutron {
+	memory-region = <&neutron_mem>;
+};
